Body:
Same behavior here, with deployment-specific details that may help.

## Environment

- opencode 1.18.14, `opencode web --port 4096 --hostname 0.0.0.0 --cors https://opencode.afonsoft.dev` (basic auth via `OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD`)
- Ubuntu 24.04.4 (aarch64) server, nginx 1.30.2 as reverse proxy (BT panel vhost, port 80 only, TLS terminated at Cloudflare)
- Full chain: **Browser (Windows 11) → Cloudflare (Flexible SSL) → cloudflared tunnel → nginx:80 → opencode:4096**

## Evidence from nginx logs

1. `opencode.afonsoft.dev.error.log`:
   ```
   upstream prematurely closed connection while reading upstream, request: "GET /global/event HTTP/1.1", upstream: "http://127.0.0.1:4096/global/event", host: "opencode.afonsoft.dev"
   ```
   `GET /global/event` is the SSE event stream that powers the live updates. When it drops mid-session, the UI freezes and only a manual refresh recovers — exactly the symptom described here.

2. Access log shows the same stream alternating between long-lived and abruptly short:
   ```
   GET /global/event 200 91996   (healthy, active session)
   GET /global/event 200 1926    (stream ended almost immediately)
   GET /global/event 200 244977  (healthy)
   GET /global/event 200 856     (stream ended almost immediately)
   ```

3. nginx location for this site does **not** disable proxy buffering:
   ```nginx
   location ^~ / {
     proxy_pass http://localhost:4096;
     proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
     proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
     proxy_connect_timeout 600s;
     proxy_send_timeout 6000s;
     proxy_read_timeout 6000s;
     proxy_http_version 1.1;
     proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
     proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
   }
   ```
   `proxy_buffering` defaults to **on**, which buffers the SSE response and can stall/delay event delivery through the proxy. With the extra cloudflared hop (`keepAliveTimeout: 15m`, `tcpKeepAlive: 120s` in the tunnel config) there are two intermediaries that can silently drop an idle/buffered SSE connection without a FIN/RST — so the client's `reader.read()` never resolves and the reconnect logic never re-enters. That matches the "spinner keeps spinning, nothing new arrives, refresh reveals the run already finished" report.

## Suggested follow-ups (proxy side + app side)

- Proxy: `proxy_buffering off;` (and `X-Accel-Buffering: no` for `text/event-stream`) for `/global/event`.
- App: the SSE consumer in the web client (see also #39352, #39030) has no liveness check — a silent socket death is never detected and `session_status` drifts. Would be good if the issue here covers the same root cause: the UI must survive a dropped/never-reconnecting event stream instead of requiring a page refresh.

Related: #39352, #39030, #38458, #32175.
